  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal, news-style term for death. Used in obituaries, news reports, and official announcements. More neutral and objective than {逝去|せいきょ}, which is an honorific term. Less formal than {逝去|せいきょ} but more formal than {亡|な}くなる (the most common everyday term for someone dying).\n\nREGISTER COMPARISON:\n- {亡|な}くなる: standard, respectful (everyday)\n- {死去|しきょ}: formal, objective (news/official)\n- {逝去|せいきょ}: honorific, respectful (very formal)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～{歳|さい}で{死去|しきょ}: died at age ~\n- {病気|びょうき}のため{死去|しきょ}: died due to illness\n- {死去|しきょ}が{報|ほう}じられる: death is reported",
